# >>> tutor-legacy-brandkit >>> (generated from BRANDKIT_* settings; do not edit here)
{#-
  TIER 2 (settings only) for the legacy, server-rendered LMS.

  Why the *production* patch: it is rendered last in the generated settings file, after
  `from lms.envs.production import *` AND after Tutor's own partials/common_lms.py, which
  itself assigns DEFAULT_EMAIL_LOGO_URL (line 22 on Tutor 21.0.9 and 22.0.2). On those
  versions the *common* patch (line 50) also renders after that assignment, so the claim
  "the common patch loses to the default" is NOT reproducible there; production is used
  because it is strictly safer regardless. See docs/VERIFICATION.md.

  What each setting drives (read from openedx-platform release/ulmo.4 + verawood.1):
    LOGO_URL            -> branding_api.get_logo_url(): the legacy header logo, which the
                           legacy dashboard inherits via main.html. Site-configuration
                           `logo_image_url` (DB) takes precedence over this setting.
    LOGO_TRADEMARK_URL  -> branding_api._footer_logo_img(): the legacy footer logo.
    FAVICON_URL         -> branding_api.get_favicon_url(): used by main.html. NOTE: the
                           root /favicon.ico route and templates extending main_django.html
                           use FAVICON_PATH (a *static* path), which a URL cannot change;
                           see BRANDKIT_BAKE_STATIC_ASSETS (Tier 1).
  No template is overridden: header.html / footer.html / dashboard.html stay stock.
-#}
{%- if BRANDKIT_ENABLE_LMS %}
{%- set _brandkit_header_logo = BRANDKIT_LOGO_PNG_URL or BRANDKIT_LOGO_SVG_URL %}
{%- if _brandkit_header_logo %}
LOGO_URL = {{ _brandkit_header_logo | brandkit_url }}
{%- endif %}
{%- set _brandkit_footer_logo = BRANDKIT_LOGO_TRADEMARK_SVG_URL or _brandkit_header_logo %}
{%- if _brandkit_footer_logo %}
LOGO_TRADEMARK_URL = {{ _brandkit_footer_logo | brandkit_url }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if BRANDKIT_FAVICON_URL %}
FAVICON_URL = {{ BRANDKIT_FAVICON_URL | brandkit_url }}
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
{% include "legacy-brandkit/partials/email-logo.py" %}
